1
00:00:00,840 --> 00:00:03,119
[♪♪]

2
00:00:03,119 --> 00:00:05,040
I'm Peppa Pig.
[SNORT]

3
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:06,920
This is my little
brother George.

4
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:08,119
[SNORTS]

5
00:00:08,119 --> 00:00:10,280
This is Mommy Pig.
[SNORTS]

6
00:00:10,280 --> 00:00:11,920
And this is Daddy Pig.

7
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:13,280
[SNORTS]
[ALL LAUGH]

8
00:00:13,280 --> 00:00:15,920
Peppa Pig.
[SNORTS]

9
00:00:17,360 --> 00:00:19,480
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

10
00:00:19,480 --> 00:00:22,000
NARRATOR:
It is the day
of the school fete.

11
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:23,959
Miss Rabbit
is running the raffle.

12
00:00:23,959 --> 00:00:25,320
Roll up! Roll up!

13
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:28,439
The top prize is a ride
in my hot air balloon.

14
00:00:28,439 --> 00:00:30,680
Wow, that sounds fun.

15
00:00:30,680 --> 00:00:33,600
[BARKS]
Can I have a ticket, please?

16
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:38,879
The blue ticket wins...
a toy car.

17
00:00:38,879 --> 00:00:41,480
Well done, Danny.

18
00:00:41,480 --> 00:00:43,199
Can I have a ticket, please?

19
00:00:43,199 --> 00:00:45,600
Thank you, Peppa.
What are you hoping to win?

20
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:47,160
The balloon ride.

21
00:00:47,160 --> 00:00:50,760
Wouldn't it be nicer to win
the homemade chocolate cake?

22
00:00:50,760 --> 00:00:53,360
Daddy Pig loves
homemade chocolate cake.

23
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:56,000
[GIGGLES]

24
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,839
The red ticket wins...

25
00:00:57,839 --> 00:00:59,680
the balloon ride!

26
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:01,040
ALL:
Hooray!

27
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:04,160
All aboard
for the balloon ride.

28
00:01:04,160 --> 00:01:06,200
How many passengers,
please?

29
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:07,440
Four, please.

30
00:01:07,440 --> 00:01:08,640
And Teddy.

31
00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:09,840
Dinosaur.

32
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:11,920
Oh, and a teddy
and a dinosaur.

33
00:01:11,920 --> 00:01:14,960
That makes six.
All aboard.

34
00:01:14,960 --> 00:01:17,080
[GIGGLING]

35
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:19,560
Hurry up, Daddy Pig.
Hop aboard.

36
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:21,119
Quick, Daddy.

37
00:01:21,119 --> 00:01:23,920
Splice the main brace.
Chocks away.

38
00:01:23,920 --> 00:01:25,560
Full steam ahead.

39
00:01:25,560 --> 00:01:27,880
Very impressive,
Miss Rabbit.

40
00:01:27,880 --> 00:01:29,880
You must be
an expert pilot.

41
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:31,320
Not really.

42
00:01:31,320 --> 00:01:33,800
This the first time
I've ever flown a balloon.

43
00:01:33,800 --> 00:01:36,440
Oh.
Hold tight.

44
00:01:36,440 --> 00:01:38,720
Miss Rabbit heats up the air
in the balloon

45
00:01:38,720 --> 00:01:40,600
to make it rise
into the sky.

46
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:41,920
Bye-bye.
Bye-bye.

47
00:01:41,920 --> 00:01:43,240
ALL:
Bye-bye!

48
00:01:44,839 --> 00:01:47,080
Would anyone like
to do the map reading?

49
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:48,280
I will.

50
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:50,160
Are you sure, Daddy Pig?
[SNORTS]

51
00:01:50,160 --> 00:01:52,800
I'm very good
at map reading.

52
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:56,600
Oh. This map
is a bit difficult.

53
00:01:56,600 --> 00:01:57,920
[ALL LAUGH]

54
00:01:57,920 --> 00:01:59,160
Shall we go higher?

55
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:00,399
Yes, please.

56
00:02:00,399 --> 00:02:01,880
Higher. Higher.

57
00:02:03,240 --> 00:02:06,679
The balloon is rising high
into the sky.

58
00:02:07,839 --> 00:02:11,079
Oh, where did
the sky go?

59
00:02:11,079 --> 00:02:12,840
DADDY PIG:
Don't worry, Peppa.

60
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:15,160
We're just flying
through a cloud.

61
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:18,280
GEORGE AND PEPPA:
Ooh!

62
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:20,920
Wow. The sky is back again.

63
00:02:20,920 --> 00:02:22,200
ALL:
Hooray!

64
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:23,480
[GIGGLES]

65
00:02:23,480 --> 00:02:26,640
♪ Big balloon, big balloon ♪

66
00:02:26,640 --> 00:02:29,840
♪ Bigger than the sun
And moon ♪

67
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:32,959
♪ Flying high in the sky ♪

68
00:02:32,959 --> 00:02:36,600
♪ Fly and fly
And fly and fly ♪

69
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:38,120
[ALL LAUGH]

70
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:41,480
Look, Teddy,
we're flying really high.

71
00:02:41,480 --> 00:02:43,720
Peppa, be careful
you don't drop--

72
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:45,400
Teddy!
I've dropped Teddy.

73
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:47,200
[MOMMY PIG GASPS]
DADDY PIG: Ooh.

74
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:49,880
Don't worry, Peppa.
We'll rescue Teddy.

75
00:02:49,880 --> 00:02:51,880
Hold tight, everybody.

76
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:54,040
We're going down.

77
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:56,600
Miss Rabbit
is making the balloon go down

78
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:58,480
so that Teddy can be rescued.

79
00:02:58,480 --> 00:03:00,760
DADDY PIG:
I can't see Teddy anywhere.

80
00:03:00,760 --> 00:03:02,160
There he is.

81
00:03:02,160 --> 00:03:04,720
Teddy's caught in a tree.

82
00:03:04,720 --> 00:03:08,519
I can use this anchor
to rescue Teddy.

83
00:03:08,519 --> 00:03:13,120
Slowly, slowly. There.

84
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:15,200
Daddy Pig
has rescued Teddy.

85
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:16,359
Teddy.

86
00:03:16,359 --> 00:03:18,399
ALL: Hooray!
[ALL LAUGH]

87
00:03:18,399 --> 00:03:21,880
Oh, dear. No one is looking
where they are going.

88
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:24,519
Look out!
Tree straight ahead!

89
00:03:24,519 --> 00:03:26,640
Hold tight.

90
00:03:28,160 --> 00:03:29,560
Ooh.

91
00:03:29,560 --> 00:03:31,840
PEPPA:
First Teddy was stuck in a tree,

92
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:34,119
and now we are stuck
in a tree.

93
00:03:34,119 --> 00:03:36,760
Daddy Pig, do you know
where we are?

94
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:37,959
Uh...

95
00:03:37,959 --> 00:03:40,119
We're lost, aren't we?

96
00:03:40,119 --> 00:03:41,280
Yes.

97
00:03:41,280 --> 00:03:42,679
Oh.
Ooh.

98
00:03:42,679 --> 00:03:44,239
Look, everyone.

99
00:03:44,239 --> 00:03:46,880
That's Granny
and Grandpa's house.

100
00:03:46,880 --> 00:03:50,480
Yes. We must be
in Grandpa Pig's garden.

101
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:51,679
As I thought.

102
00:03:51,679 --> 00:03:56,359
Ahoy there, Granny Pig
and Grandpa Pig!

103
00:03:56,359 --> 00:04:00,560
Goodness me.
Ahoy there, Miss Rabbit!

104
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:03,239
Uh, help. Please.

105
00:04:03,239 --> 00:04:07,640
Grandpa,
we can't get down!

106
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:10,720
Don't worry.
I've got a ladder.

107
00:04:10,720 --> 00:04:12,239
ALL:
Hooray!

108
00:04:12,239 --> 00:04:15,079
Everyone climbs down
from the big balloon.

109
00:04:15,079 --> 00:04:17,079
Granny, Grandpa!

110
00:04:17,079 --> 00:04:19,479
Miss Rabbit took us
for a ride

111
00:04:19,479 --> 00:04:21,240
in her big balloon.

112
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:22,840
How very exciting.

113
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:26,240
I'm afraid the most
exciting thing we can offer

114
00:04:26,240 --> 00:04:29,240
is a piece of my homemade
chocolate cake.

115
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:32,760
Homemade chocolate cake.
That is exciting.

116
00:04:32,760 --> 00:04:36,440
[GIGGLES]
That was the best
balloon ride ever.

117
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:40,200
Mmm. And that was
the best chocolate cake ever.

118
00:04:40,200 --> 00:04:41,440
[CHUCKLES]

119
00:04:41,440 --> 00:04:43,520
[ALL LAUGHING]

120
00:04:49,440 --> 00:04:51,880
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

121
00:04:51,880 --> 00:04:54,240
NARRATOR:
Today is George's birthday.

122
00:04:54,240 --> 00:04:55,840
[ROOSTER CROWS]

123
00:04:55,840 --> 00:04:58,800
It is very early
in the morning.

124
00:04:58,800 --> 00:05:00,840
[SNORTS]

125
00:05:00,840 --> 00:05:03,800
[GIGGLING]

126
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:06,640
George,
it's too early.

127
00:05:06,640 --> 00:05:08,880
Dinosaur. Grrr.

128
00:05:08,880 --> 00:05:11,919
Go back to bed.
[GIGGLES]

129
00:05:11,919 --> 00:05:15,240
It sounds like someone's
up bright and early.

130
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:16,400
[SNORTS]

131
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:18,440
BOTH:
Happy Birthday, George.

132
00:05:18,440 --> 00:05:20,080
George woke me up.

133
00:05:20,080 --> 00:05:23,120
You woke everyone up
on your birthday, Peppa.

134
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:26,400
That was different.
That was my birthday.

135
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:29,640
And today is
George's birthday.

136
00:05:29,640 --> 00:05:30,919
[YAWNS]

137
00:05:30,919 --> 00:05:32,520
Happy Birthday,
George.

138
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:34,280
[GIGGLES AND SNORTS]

139
00:05:35,479 --> 00:05:37,359
Here's your present,
George.

140
00:05:37,359 --> 00:05:38,599
[SNORTS]

141
00:05:38,599 --> 00:05:39,880
[RATTLES]

142
00:05:39,880 --> 00:05:42,320
Ooh.

143
00:05:42,320 --> 00:05:44,080
[SNORTS]
Dinosaur!

144
00:05:44,080 --> 00:05:45,520
[GIGGLES]

145
00:05:45,520 --> 00:05:49,000
I knew it would be
some sort of dinosaur thingy.

146
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:50,880
Grrr.

147
00:05:50,880 --> 00:05:53,680
[CHUCKLES]
Squeeze its tummy.

148
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:55,320
[TOY ROARS]
Eek!

149
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:56,560
Too scary.

150
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:58,320
[ALL LAUGH]

151
00:05:58,320 --> 00:06:01,719
George, I've made you
a birthday card.

152
00:06:01,719 --> 00:06:05,000
Can you guess
what the picture is?

153
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,560
George cannot guess.

154
00:06:06,560 --> 00:06:09,200
I was going
to paint you a flower.

155
00:06:09,200 --> 00:06:10,440
Oh.

156
00:06:10,440 --> 00:06:12,719
George does not like flowers.

157
00:06:12,719 --> 00:06:15,840
But in the end,
I painted you a...

158
00:06:15,840 --> 00:06:17,039
Dinosaur!

159
00:06:17,039 --> 00:06:19,400
That's a lovely
picture, Peppa.

160
00:06:19,400 --> 00:06:22,560
Yes. I'm very good
at painting.

161
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:25,039
Now we're going
somewhere very special

162
00:06:25,039 --> 00:06:27,240
for George's
birthday treat.

163
00:06:27,240 --> 00:06:30,440
Yippee! Let's go.

164
00:06:30,440 --> 00:06:31,919
Where are we going?

165
00:06:31,919 --> 00:06:34,000
[SNORTS]
You'll see.

166
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,760
[GEORGE GIGGLES]

167
00:06:35,760 --> 00:06:38,960
The family are setting off
for George's birthday treat.

168
00:06:38,960 --> 00:06:40,240
[HORN BEEPS]

169
00:06:42,039 --> 00:06:43,919
Are we going
to the circus?

170
00:06:43,919 --> 00:06:47,000
No, but it's somewhere
just as good.

171
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:49,120
Um, is it the cinema?

172
00:06:49,120 --> 00:06:51,440
DADDY PIG:
No. Much better.

173
00:06:51,440 --> 00:06:53,719
I just can't guess.

174
00:06:53,719 --> 00:06:55,840
Where can they be going?

175
00:06:56,840 --> 00:06:58,719
DADDY PIG:
We're here!

176
00:06:58,719 --> 00:07:00,719
The family have arrived
at the museum.

177
00:07:00,719 --> 00:07:02,640
Why are we
at the museum?

178
00:07:02,640 --> 00:07:04,520
Come on, you'll see.

179
00:07:04,520 --> 00:07:09,120
What can George's
birthday treat be?

180
00:07:09,120 --> 00:07:13,880
George, what do you like best
in the whole world?

181
00:07:13,880 --> 00:07:15,359
Dinosaur.

182
00:07:15,359 --> 00:07:16,799
[GIGGLES]

183
00:07:16,799 --> 00:07:20,719
Ooh, dinosaur.

184
00:07:20,719 --> 00:07:22,799
George's birthday treat
is a visit

185
00:07:22,799 --> 00:07:25,120
to the museum dinosaur room.

186
00:07:25,120 --> 00:07:28,919
Huh. Silly old
dinosaurs again.

187
00:07:28,919 --> 00:07:32,359
[GIGGLING]

188
00:07:32,359 --> 00:07:34,200
Dinosaur.

189
00:07:34,200 --> 00:07:35,880
[BEEPS]
[ROARS]

190
00:07:35,880 --> 00:07:37,120
[GASPS]

191
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:38,719
[CRIES]

192
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:41,280
Don't be frightened,
George.

193
00:07:41,280 --> 00:07:43,159
It's not
a real dinosaur.

194
00:07:43,159 --> 00:07:45,080
It's just a robot.

195
00:07:45,080 --> 00:07:48,400
Look, I stand
on this spot and...

196
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:50,799
[BEEPS]
[ROARS]

197
00:07:50,799 --> 00:07:52,479
[GIGGLES]

198
00:07:53,840 --> 00:07:56,239
[BEEPS]
[ROARS]

199
00:07:56,239 --> 00:07:57,880
[GIGGLES]

200
00:07:57,880 --> 00:07:59,840
Grrr!

201
00:07:59,840 --> 00:08:01,679
[ALL LAUGH]

202
00:08:01,679 --> 00:08:03,479
And now there's another
surprise.

203
00:08:03,479 --> 00:08:06,960
All of George and Peppa's
friends are here.

204
00:08:06,960 --> 00:08:09,719
ALL:
Surprise!

205
00:08:09,719 --> 00:08:12,479
Mommy Rabbit has made
a birthday cake for George.

206
00:08:12,479 --> 00:08:15,679
Can anyone guess
what sort cake it is?

207
00:08:15,679 --> 00:08:17,440
A dinosaur cake?

208
00:08:17,440 --> 00:08:21,239
It is!
What an amazing guess, Peppa.

209
00:08:21,239 --> 00:08:23,200
ALL:
Happy Birthday, George!

210
00:08:23,200 --> 00:08:24,440
[GIGGLES]

211
00:08:24,440 --> 00:08:26,599
There's one last surprise.

212
00:08:26,599 --> 00:08:28,560
Follow me.

213
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:31,840
What is the last surprise?

214
00:08:31,840 --> 00:08:34,559
What do you think it is,
Peppa.

215
00:08:34,559 --> 00:08:39,000
It's probably something
to do with dinosaurs.

216
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,959
Oh. What's that?
[LAUGHS]

217
00:08:41,959 --> 00:08:45,840
It just needs
to be filled with air.

218
00:08:45,840 --> 00:08:49,600
I know, I know.
It's a bouncy castle.

219
00:08:49,600 --> 00:08:51,880
Peppa loves bouncy castles.

220
00:08:51,880 --> 00:08:53,520
But if it's for George,

221
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:57,040
why isn't it something
to do with dinosaurs?

222
00:08:57,040 --> 00:08:59,880
Ho-ho!
It is a dinosaur.

223
00:08:59,880 --> 00:09:01,680
A bouncy dinosaur.

224
00:09:01,680 --> 00:09:03,360
ALL:
Hooray!

225
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:05,360
[ALL LAUGHING]

226
00:09:05,360 --> 00:09:07,840
George loves
bouncy dinosaurs.

227
00:09:07,840 --> 00:09:11,480
Everyone loves
bouncy dinosaurs.

228
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:13,120
This is great.

229
00:09:13,120 --> 00:09:15,240
Happy birthday, George.

230
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:16,880
[LAUGHS]
[SNORTS]

231
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:23,000
[PEPPA READS ONSCREEN TEXT]

232
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:26,000
NARRATOR:
Suzy Sheep has come
to play with Peppa.

233
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:27,959
[BLEATS AND LAUGHS]

234
00:09:27,959 --> 00:09:29,800
Hello, Peppa.

235
00:09:29,800 --> 00:09:31,360
Hello, Suzy.

236
00:09:31,360 --> 00:09:36,160
This is my new friend,
Leo Lion.

237
00:09:36,160 --> 00:09:39,120
Where is he?
There's no one there.

238
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:41,800
Suzy has made up
a pretend friend.

239
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:43,920
Can't you see him, Peppa?

240
00:09:43,920 --> 00:09:46,600
Um...
[GIGGLES]

241
00:09:46,600 --> 00:09:48,600
Let's play catch.

242
00:09:48,600 --> 00:09:52,160
Okay. To you, Leo.

243
00:09:52,160 --> 00:09:55,319
Peppa throws the ball
to Suzy's pretend friend.

244
00:09:55,319 --> 00:09:57,439
Leo can't catch the ball.

245
00:09:57,439 --> 00:10:01,160
He can. He just doesn't
like playing catch.

246
00:10:01,160 --> 00:10:03,520
What does Leo
like doing?

247
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:05,520
He likes to roar.

248
00:10:05,520 --> 00:10:07,920
Is he going to roar now?

249
00:10:07,920 --> 00:10:11,160
Um, yes. Ahem.

250
00:10:11,160 --> 00:10:12,920
Roar.

251
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:14,800
Wasn't that you?

252
00:10:14,800 --> 00:10:16,920
No, that was Leo.

253
00:10:16,920 --> 00:10:19,600
Ah. Hello, Leo.

254
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:22,480
Peppa pretends
that she can see Leo Lion.

255
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:26,439
Leo, will you be
my friend too?

256
00:10:26,439 --> 00:10:27,920
[WHISPERS]
What did he say?

257
00:10:27,920 --> 00:10:30,040
He's nodding his head.

258
00:10:30,040 --> 00:10:32,680
That means yes.

259
00:10:32,680 --> 00:10:34,520
Peppa, Suzy,

260
00:10:34,520 --> 00:10:38,959
would you like to come inside
and have some fruit cake?

261
00:10:38,959 --> 00:10:43,319
Mommy Pig has two slices of
fruit cake for Suzy and Peppa.

262
00:10:43,319 --> 00:10:46,400
Mommy, Suzy's got
a pretend friend.

263
00:10:46,400 --> 00:10:48,720
He's called Leo Lion.

264
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:52,040
I see. And does he
like fruit cake too?

265
00:10:52,040 --> 00:10:55,079
Roar!
Leo loves fruit cake.

266
00:10:55,079 --> 00:10:56,920
Don't be silly, Peppa.

267
00:10:56,920 --> 00:11:01,000
That wasn't Leo,
that was you.

268
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:04,360
Leo prefers
chocolate cake.

269
00:11:04,360 --> 00:11:08,240
I haven't got chocolate cake.
Will Leo have some fruit cake?

270
00:11:08,240 --> 00:11:12,560
Roar. He will try
a little slice.

271
00:11:12,560 --> 00:11:17,280
Mommy Pig gives some cake
to Suzy's pretend friend.

272
00:11:17,280 --> 00:11:20,760
George is playing
with Mr. Dinosaur.

273
00:11:20,760 --> 00:11:23,079
Dinosaur. Grrr.

274
00:11:23,079 --> 00:11:25,959
George, you're sitting
on Leo.

275
00:11:25,959 --> 00:11:29,120
George does not know that Suzy
has made up a friend.

276
00:11:29,120 --> 00:11:31,400
Roar!

277
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:33,400
[CRIES]

278
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:37,800
Um, Leo Lion says
he can't finish his cake,

279
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:39,439
so George can have it.

280
00:11:39,439 --> 00:11:40,640
[SNORTS]

281
00:11:40,640 --> 00:11:42,040
[BOTH LAUGH]

282
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:44,959
[GIGGLES]

283
00:11:44,959 --> 00:11:47,040
Can we play upstairs now?

284
00:11:47,040 --> 00:11:49,319
Yes. Let's play
dressing up.

285
00:11:49,319 --> 00:11:52,839
I was asking Leo.
Oh.

286
00:11:52,839 --> 00:11:54,680
Roar!

287
00:11:54,680 --> 00:11:57,600
Leo says he likes
playing dressing up.

288
00:11:57,600 --> 00:11:58,839
Good.

289
00:11:58,839 --> 00:12:02,560
Come on, Leo.

290
00:12:02,560 --> 00:12:05,480
Peppa and Suzy
are playing dressing up.

291
00:12:05,480 --> 00:12:07,520
Peppa is going
to be a fairy.

292
00:12:07,520 --> 00:12:09,800
I grant you one wish.

293
00:12:09,800 --> 00:12:13,120
My wish is
to be Queen Suzy.

294
00:12:13,120 --> 00:12:16,600
And Leo Lion
will be the jester.

295
00:12:16,600 --> 00:12:18,920
He doesn't want
to be the jester.

296
00:12:18,920 --> 00:12:21,199
He wants to be the king.

297
00:12:21,199 --> 00:12:22,880
Here is Daddy Pig.

298
00:12:22,880 --> 00:12:26,760
Mommy Pig tells me
you have a very special visitor.

299
00:12:26,760 --> 00:12:29,520
It's only Suzy,
Daddy.

300
00:12:29,520 --> 00:12:32,439
Are you sure there isn't
someone else, Peppa?

301
00:12:32,439 --> 00:12:36,000
There is someone else:
King Leo Lion.

302
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:37,760
Roar!

303
00:12:37,760 --> 00:12:38,920
[CHUCKLES]

304
00:12:38,920 --> 00:12:40,920
It's an honor
to meet you, King Leo.

305
00:12:40,920 --> 00:12:43,959
Daddy Pig pretends
he can see King Leo.

306
00:12:43,959 --> 00:12:47,280
May I say what a fine
golden mane you have?

307
00:12:47,280 --> 00:12:49,439
Yes, it is very fine.

308
00:12:49,439 --> 00:12:52,480
And he is wearing
his best red trousers.

309
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:54,079
Oh, yes.

310
00:12:54,079 --> 00:12:56,040
And his blue jumper.

311
00:12:56,040 --> 00:13:00,079
Silly Peppa. Leo isn't
wearing a blue jumper.

312
00:13:00,079 --> 00:13:03,240
He's wearing
his best green shirt.

313
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:06,560
Well, it is sort
of a bluey-green.

314
00:13:06,560 --> 00:13:08,160
[BOTH GIGGLE]

315
00:13:08,160 --> 00:13:10,920
Peppa, Suzy,
your friends are here.

316
00:13:10,920 --> 00:13:12,880
Peppa's friends are here.

317
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:14,880
They are all wearing
their boots.

318
00:13:14,880 --> 00:13:17,040
Let's jump
in muddy puddles.

319
00:13:17,040 --> 00:13:18,280
BOTH:
Yes!

320
00:13:18,280 --> 00:13:20,079
[ALL LAUGHING]

321
00:13:24,719 --> 00:13:27,240
Are you sure
Leo should jump in puddles

322
00:13:27,240 --> 00:13:28,839
without his boots?

323
00:13:28,839 --> 00:13:30,000
Oh, I forgot.

324
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:32,599
Leo's wearing his boots
as well.

325
00:13:32,599 --> 00:13:35,040
[LAUGHS]
Look at Leo.

326
00:13:35,040 --> 00:13:37,599
He's jumping
up and down too.

327
00:13:37,599 --> 00:13:39,520
Roar!

328
00:13:39,520 --> 00:13:43,560
Everyone loves jumping
up and down in muddy puddles,

329
00:13:43,560 --> 00:13:45,400
even pretend friends.

330
00:13:45,400 --> 00:13:47,880
Roar!

331
00:13:50,480 --> 00:13:53,240
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

332
00:13:53,240 --> 00:13:56,439
NARRATOR:
Peppa and George
are painting today.

333
00:13:56,439 --> 00:13:59,839
We need some old newspaper
to put on the table.

334
00:13:59,839 --> 00:14:01,400
Yes.
[SNORTS]

335
00:14:01,400 --> 00:14:03,439
Daddy Pig is reading
his newspaper.

336
00:14:03,439 --> 00:14:05,680
You can have
my newspaper

337
00:14:05,680 --> 00:14:07,920
when I've finished
reading it.

338
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:12,280
All right,
here you are, George.

339
00:14:12,280 --> 00:14:14,160
Hooray!

340
00:14:14,160 --> 00:14:17,160
Now we can start
painting.

341
00:14:20,439 --> 00:14:22,079
Silly George.

342
00:14:22,079 --> 00:14:26,000
Big children do not put
their hands in the paint.

343
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:27,400
[GIGGLES]

344
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:30,160
George loves painting
with his hands.

345
00:14:32,680 --> 00:14:34,079
[LAUGHS]

346
00:14:34,079 --> 00:14:36,199
Peppa loves painting
with her hands.

347
00:14:36,199 --> 00:14:37,839
[BOTH GIGGLE]

348
00:14:37,839 --> 00:14:39,240
Very good.

349
00:14:39,240 --> 00:14:41,920
Can I have a potato,
Mommy Pig?

350
00:14:41,920 --> 00:14:44,280
They aren't cooked yet,
Daddy Pig.

351
00:14:44,280 --> 00:14:46,160
Are you hungry,
Daddy?

352
00:14:46,160 --> 00:14:50,560
I'm not going to eat it.
Watch this.

353
00:14:50,560 --> 00:14:52,920
What is Daddy Pig doing?

354
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:56,400
BOTH:
Ooh.

355
00:14:56,400 --> 00:14:59,319
Now, who can tell me
what this is?

356
00:15:02,160 --> 00:15:03,640
A flower.

357
00:15:03,640 --> 00:15:04,839
[ALL LAUGH]

358
00:15:04,839 --> 00:15:06,760
Clever Daddy.
[CHUCKLES]

359
00:15:06,760 --> 00:15:09,599
I loved painting
when I was a young piggy.

360
00:15:09,599 --> 00:15:12,280
Now, where are
my old painting things?

361
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:14,280
[GIGGLES]

362
00:15:14,280 --> 00:15:17,880
Daddy, why are you
wearing that funny hat?

363
00:15:17,880 --> 00:15:19,120
[LAUGHS]

364
00:15:19,120 --> 00:15:21,959
This is my beret.

365
00:15:21,959 --> 00:15:24,920
It puts me in the mood
for painting pictures.

366
00:15:26,400 --> 00:15:29,319
Now, what shall I paint?

367
00:15:29,319 --> 00:15:31,520
[GIGGLES AND SNORTS]

368
00:15:31,520 --> 00:15:33,360
Well chosen, George.

369
00:15:33,360 --> 00:15:36,199
I'll paint
the old cherry tree.

370
00:15:36,199 --> 00:15:39,000
What's that?

371
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:42,400
It's an easel, Peppa.
It holds my canvas.

372
00:15:42,400 --> 00:15:44,199
What's a canvas?

373
00:15:44,199 --> 00:15:48,599
It's a bit like paper,
for very special paintings.

374
00:15:48,599 --> 00:15:50,400
Is that
toothpaste?

375
00:15:50,400 --> 00:15:51,640
[LAUGHS]

376
00:15:51,640 --> 00:15:53,040
No, Peppa.

377
00:15:53,040 --> 00:15:56,599
These are special paints
for grown-up artists.

378
00:15:59,880 --> 00:16:02,680
There. What color
shall we begin with?

379
00:16:02,680 --> 00:16:03,959
Red, please.

380
00:16:03,959 --> 00:16:05,560
Why red, Peppa?

381
00:16:05,560 --> 00:16:08,000
Red is
my favorite color.

382
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:10,760
But first we need
to paint the sky.

383
00:16:10,760 --> 00:16:12,560
Look. What color is it?

384
00:16:12,560 --> 00:16:14,280
Blue of course

385
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:15,800
DADDY PIG:
Very good.

386
00:16:15,800 --> 00:16:17,839
Let's start with blue.

387
00:16:17,839 --> 00:16:19,280
[BOTH GIGGLE]

388
00:16:19,280 --> 00:16:21,120
Now for the cherry tree.

389
00:16:21,120 --> 00:16:22,680
We need green
for the leaves.

390
00:16:22,680 --> 00:16:24,800
PEPPA:
But there isn't any green.

391
00:16:24,800 --> 00:16:26,319
DADDY PIG:
Never mind.

392
00:16:26,319 --> 00:16:29,120
If we mix blue paint
with yellow paint,

393
00:16:29,120 --> 00:16:30,680
we can make green.

394
00:16:30,680 --> 00:16:32,800
Mixing blue and yellow
makes green.

395
00:16:32,800 --> 00:16:34,319
GEORGE AND PEPPA:
Ooh.

396
00:16:34,319 --> 00:16:36,880
What lovely
green leaves.

397
00:16:36,880 --> 00:16:38,800
And here's some grass.

398
00:16:38,800 --> 00:16:40,560
What about
the branches?

399
00:16:40,560 --> 00:16:43,000
We haven't got
brown paint.

400
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:44,520
We can make brown.

401
00:16:44,520 --> 00:16:47,079
We'll mix the green
and the red.

402
00:16:47,079 --> 00:16:49,120
Mixing green and red
makes brown.

403
00:16:49,120 --> 00:16:50,800
GEORGE AND PEPPA:
Ooh.

404
00:16:50,800 --> 00:16:54,240
Daddy Pig paints the tree trunk
and the branches.

405
00:16:54,240 --> 00:16:55,680
BOTH:
Wow.

406
00:16:55,680 --> 00:16:57,160
[GIGGLES]
Daddy,

407
00:16:57,160 --> 00:16:58,520
can I paint the cherries?

408
00:16:58,520 --> 00:17:00,079
Yes, Peppa.

409
00:17:00,079 --> 00:17:03,479
Put your finger in the paint
and dab it onto the tree.

410
00:17:03,479 --> 00:17:04,680
[GIGGLES]

411
00:17:04,680 --> 00:17:07,440
One... two... three.

412
00:17:07,440 --> 00:17:08,879
DADDY PIG:
Well done.

413
00:17:08,879 --> 00:17:10,720
Now it's
George's turn.

414
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:14,280
[GIGGLES]

415
00:17:14,280 --> 00:17:17,280
What a great painter
you are, George.

416
00:17:17,280 --> 00:17:18,440
[SNORTS AND LAUGHS]

417
00:17:18,440 --> 00:17:21,040
There.
The painting is finished.

418
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:22,599
Hooray!
[SNORTS]

419
00:17:22,599 --> 00:17:23,760
[QUACKING]

420
00:17:23,760 --> 00:17:26,000
Oh, it's the ducks.

421
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:27,200
Hello, Mrs. Duck.

422
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:30,280
We're painting
a picture.

423
00:17:30,280 --> 00:17:32,760
The ducks are running
through Daddy's paint.

424
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:35,919
Shoo! Shoo!
Naughty ducks.

425
00:17:35,919 --> 00:17:37,120
Shoo, ducks!
Shoo!

426
00:17:37,120 --> 00:17:38,800
Stay away
from our painting.

427
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:41,000
Whoa!

428
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:42,520
[QUACKING]

429
00:17:42,520 --> 00:17:45,280
Oh, no, the ducks
have made paint footprints

430
00:17:45,280 --> 00:17:47,520
all over the painting.

431
00:17:47,520 --> 00:17:49,040
Oh, dear.

432
00:17:49,040 --> 00:17:50,879
What was all that noise?

433
00:17:50,879 --> 00:17:55,200
Mommy, the ducks
have spoiled our painting.

434
00:17:55,200 --> 00:17:57,639
Hmm, let me see.

435
00:17:57,639 --> 00:18:00,440
The ducks are making
paint footprints in the garden,

436
00:18:00,440 --> 00:18:02,280
just like the ones
on the painting.

437
00:18:02,280 --> 00:18:04,800
Daddy's painting
isn't spoiled, Peppa.

438
00:18:04,800 --> 00:18:06,520
It's perfect.

439
00:18:06,520 --> 00:18:07,879
Hooray!
[SNORTS]

440
00:18:07,879 --> 00:18:09,240
Oh, yes.

441
00:18:09,240 --> 00:18:12,000
I am a bit of an expert
at painting.

442
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:13,960
And so are the ducks.

443
00:18:13,960 --> 00:18:15,440
[ALL QUACKING]

444
00:18:15,440 --> 00:18:17,520
[ALL LAUGHING]

445
00:18:18,879 --> 00:18:21,320
[♪♪]

446
00:18:21,320 --> 00:18:22,919
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

447
00:18:22,919 --> 00:18:26,280
[SNORTS, GIGGLES]

448
00:18:26,280 --> 00:18:27,520
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

449
00:18:27,520 --> 00:18:29,960
[SNORTS, GIGGLES]

450
00:18:29,960 --> 00:18:32,280
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

451
00:18:32,280 --> 00:18:33,639
[SNORTS]

